---
import LegalLayout from "../layouts/LegalLayout.astro";

const base = import.meta.env.BASE_URL.replace(/\/$/, "");
---

<LegalLayout
  title="Cookies Policy — CG Design & Co."
  description="What this site stores in your browser and why: no tracking, analytics or advertising cookies."
  pageTitle="Cookies Policy"
  lastUpdated="20 November 2026"
>
  <h2>The short version</h2>
  <p>
    This site doesn't use tracking, advertising or analytics cookies. It
    doesn't build a profile of you or sell data to anyone. The only things
    it stores are strictly necessary for the site to work, which is why we
    don't ask you to accept them.
  </p>

  <h2>What we store</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>
      <strong>Cookie notice</strong> (<code>cg-cookie-consent</code>, in your
      browser's local storage) — remembers that you've seen the notice about
      cookies, so it isn't shown again. Kept until you clear your browser
      data.
    </li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Spam protection on the contact form</h2>
  <p>
    When you start filling in the contact form, we load
    <a href="https://www.hcaptcha.com/privacy" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">hCaptcha</a>,
    a spam check run by Intuition Machines, Inc. It may set a cookie or use
    local storage, and it looks at device and interaction data, such as
    mouse and keyboard activity, to tell people from bots. It only loads
    once you use the form, and it's strictly necessary to send your enquiry
    safely. Your details are then delivered to us by Web3Forms.
  </p>

  <h2>Other sites</h2>
  <p>
    Our fonts are hosted on this site, so loading a page doesn't contact
    Google or any other font service. If you pay us through Stripe, follow a
    link to WhatsApp, Google or a client's website, those sites set their
    own cookies under their own policies.
  </p>

  <h2>If that changes</h2>
  <p>
    If we ever add analytics or advertising tools, we'll update this page
    and ask for your consent before they run. Nothing like that will load
    until you've said yes.
  </p>

  <h2>Controlling storage yourself</h2>
  <p>
    You can clear cookies and local storage for this site at any time in
    your browser's settings. The cookie notice will then show again on your
    next visit. See our <a href={`${base}/privacy-policy/`}>Privacy Policy</a>
    for how we use personal data.
  </p>
</LegalLayout>
